  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Since \\(x^2-1=(x-1)(x+1)\\), each denominator factor, \\(x-1\\) and \\(x+1\\), is needed only once. Therefore, the least common denominator is \\((x-1)(x+1)=x^2-1\\).",
